From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0396-mac-lead-02-upscale-keep-drawn-frame.patch

Source: 0396-mac-lead-02-upscale-keep-drawn-frame.patch
video_core: EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_KEEP_FRAME and _TRACE for Ocarina's gameplay stand-in

EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_KEEP_FRAME=1 keeps an E5B9G9R9 input in the stand-in upscale. Movies and the title
are unchanged: their input is format 9 and is still replaced by the decoded picture.
EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_TRACE=1 logs each change of a program's input with sizes and formats, at most 64
lines. Unset, nothing changes.

Why: 0048 replaces an image "only the rejected passes fill". That holds for the movies. In gameplay
the swap also fires: run40, 55, 62, 66 and 68 all log format 33 replacing 0x8113971000 format 32.
run68 logs game draws into 0x8113971000 at 1920x1080, so that image is not filled only by rejected
passes. kraibse's "as bright as the network's own output" check in 0040 predates 0048.

The substitute is another image: its slot moves (+0xe8 in run68, +0xfc in run66) and its address too
(0x8115776000, 0x8114456000, 0x8114487000). The handle scan of the program's code doesn't list it,
or the search above the swap would have taken it first. What it holds is not known. The program's
first dispatch at 76.9 s was not swapped, the swap was first logged at 79.4 s.

Guess, not proven: the wrong image reaches the screen and this is part of the glitches on camera
moves or of the white. The trace shows whether the input changes from frame to frame. The swap
log stops at one line per program and the blit log at four lines, so no log shows it today.

Checked off the console: PS5-target clang syntax check. Applies on core16, and after next18's 0210,
0320 and 0334, the only later patches that touch this file or lower_to_maxwell.h.

Core patch. Nothing here has run on a console.

diff --git a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
index b8572f132e..9eb5943beb 100644
--- a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
@@ -993,7 +993,13 @@ bool KeplerCompute::UpscaleInsteadOfNativeProgram() {
         // The last pass of a rejected network can read an image only the rejected passes fill
         // (Ocarina of Time's title and movies): the frame is then another image of that size in
         // cbuf0 that upscales to the same output, which is what the scan below used to find.
-        for (u32 slot = 0x80; input && slot < 0x120; slot += 4) {
+        // EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_KEEP_FRAME=1 leaves an E5B9G9R9 input alone. That is Ocarina of Time's
+        // gameplay frame: draws fill it (run68), so the reason above doesn't apply to it, and
+        // without this it gives way to a B10G11R11 image its handle scan doesn't list.
+        static const bool keep_drawn_frame = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_KEEP_FRAME") != nullptr;
+        const bool keep_input =
+            keep_drawn_frame && input && input->format == Texture::TextureFormat::E5B9G9R9;
+        for (u32 slot = 0x80; input && !keep_input && slot < 0x120; slot += 4) {
             const auto from = memory_manager.Read<u32>(cbuf_address + slot) != 0 ? image(slot)
                                                                                     : std::nullopt;
             if (!upscale_pair(from, output) || from->Address() == input->Address() ||
@@ -1034,6 +1040,22 @@ bool KeplerCompute::UpscaleInsteadOfNativeProgram() {
             }
         }
     }
+    // EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_TRACE=1 logs each change of a program's input (at most 64 lines): the log
+    // below stops after four blits, so it never reaches Ocarina of Time's gameplay program.
+    if (static const bool trace = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_TRACE") != nullptr;
+        trace && input && output) {
+        static std::unordered_map<GPUVAddr, GPUVAddr> inputs;
+        static u32 changes{};
+        GPUVAddr& previous = inputs[regs.code_loc.Address()];
+        if (previous != input->Address() && changes < 64) {
+            ++changes;
+            LOG_INFO(HW_GPU, "Upscale fallback for program {:#x}: input {:#x} format {} {}x{}, output {:#x} format {} {}x{}",
+                     regs.code_loc.Address(), input->Address(), static_cast<u32>(input->format.Value()),
+                     input->Width(), input->Height(), output->Address(),
+                     static_cast<u32>(output->format.Value()), output->Width(), output->Height());
+        }
+        previous = input->Address();
+    }
     const auto skip = [&](std::string_view reason) {
         static std::unordered_set<GPUVAddr> reported;
         if (reported.insert(regs.code_loc.Address()).second && reported.size() <= 64) {
